    </div>
    <p class="section-sub">
      Data-protection law gives you a set of rights. Most of them, here, resolve to a button
      in your own browser, which is a good sign rather than a dodge.
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Bleepboard holds no accounts and keeps no user records, so there is normally nothing
        on our side to look up, correct, export or erase. The favourites list is already
        yours: it is on your device, we cannot see it, and you can delete it yourself in
